(mo-definition GO--0000304 "&quot;A change in state or activity of a cell or an organism (in terms of movement, secretion, enzyme production, gene expression, etc.) as a result of a singlet oxygen stimulus. Singlet oxygen is a dioxygen (O2) molecule in which two 2p electrons have similar spin. Singlet oxygen is more highly reactive than the form in which these electrons are of opposite spin, and it is produced in mutant chloroplasts lacking carotenoids and by leukocytes during metabolic burst.&quot; [GOC:krc, ISBN:0124325653, ISBN:0198506732 &quot;Oxford Dictionary of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology&quot;]")

